  <section class="sdr-definition-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">The service, explained</div>
      <h2>What are outsourced SDR and BDR services?</h2>
      <p class="sdr-section-intro"><strong>Outsourced SDR and BDR services give your company a managed team for finding, reaching, and qualifying potential buyers.</strong> CallTeam runs the agreed work before the sales meeting. Your team owns discovery, proposals, negotiation, and closing.</p>
      <div class="sdr-definition-grid">
        <article><span class="sdr-card-kicker">SDR · Sales development representative</span><h3>Develop and qualify sales conversations.</h3><p>SDR work can cover outbound prospects or incoming leads: research, outreach, response handling, follow-up, qualification, and scheduling.</p></article>
        <article><span class="sdr-card-kicker">BDR · Business development representative</span><h3>Open conversations with new accounts.</h3><p>BDR work often focuses on new-business outbound: choose suitable companies, find the right people, introduce the offer, and build interest.</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="sdr-plain-note">Titles vary by company and the responsibilities overlap. We agree exactly what your campaign needs, who owns it, and what makes a meeting qualified.</p>
      <p class="sdr-inline-reading">Looking specifically for booked meetings? See <a href="/services/b2b-appointment-setting/">B2B appointment setting</a>. Need someone to work incoming inquiries? Read our <a href="/articles/outsourced-inbound-lead-follow-up/">inbound lead follow-up guide</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

