  <section id="sdr-process" class="sdr-launch-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">How SDR and BDR outsourcing works</div>
      <h2>One connected process, from your offer to the handoff.</h2>
      <p class="sdr-section-intro">You should know what happens before, during, and after the calls. We agree the audience, message, systems, and qualification standard before execution.</p>
      <div class="sdr-launch-panel">
        <div class="sdr-launch-head"><span>YOUR CAMPAIGN WORKFLOW</span><strong>PREPARE · EXECUTE · IMPROVE</strong></div>
        <div class="sdr-launch-grid">
          <article><small>01 · UNDERSTAND</small><h3>Learn your offer</h3><p>Define the buyer's problem, your proof, approved claims, objections, and reason to act.</p></article>
          <article><small>02 · PREPARE</small><h3>Build the campaign</h3><p>Confirm accounts, contacts, talk track, follow-up, qualification, CRM fields, and calendars.</p></article>
          <article class="active"><small>03 · REACH</small><h3>Work the market</h3><p>Call, listen, handle responses and referrals, and follow up through agreed channels.</p></article>
          <article><small>04 · QUALIFY</small><h3>Book with context</h3><p>Confirm fit and purpose, schedule the meeting, and pass useful notes to your team.</p></article>
          <article><small>05 · REFINE</small><h3>Use what we learn</h3><p>Review response patterns, data quality, buyer language, and opportunities to improve.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="sdr-operating-system" class="sdr-responsibility-grid">
        <article><h3>CallTeam manages</h3><p>The agreed research, list work, calling, follow-up, response handling, qualification, scheduling, reporting, and campaign improvements.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Your company owns</h3><p>The offer, pricing, product knowledge, approved proof, key campaign decisions, sales availability, and the work required to close.</p></article>
