  <section id="faq" class="sdr-faq-section">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="section-label">Outsourced SDR and BDR FAQ</div>
      <h2>Direct answers before you outsource sales development.</h2>
      <div class="sdr-faq-list">
        <details open><summary>What are outsourced SDR services?</summary><p>Outsourced SDR services give a company a managed sales development function. CallTeam handles agreed targeting, research, calling, follow-up, qualification, meeting scheduling, CRM handoff, and reporting. Your team owns discovery, proposals, negotiation, and closing.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What are outsourced BDR services?</summary><p>Outsourced BDR services focus on finding and developing new business opportunities. CallTeam identifies suitable companies and buyers, opens outbound conversations, follows up, qualifies the response, and arranges an agreed next step with your sales team.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What is the difference between an SDR and a BDR?</summary><p>SDR means sales development representative. BDR means business development representative. Companies use the titles differently: SDR can cover inbound or outbound development, while BDR often refers to new-business outbound prospecting. Responsibilities overlap, so CallTeam defines the work and meeting standard before launch.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How is SDR outsourcing different from appointment setting?</summary><p>Appointment setting focuses on earning and scheduling qualified sales meetings. SDR outsourcing covers the work around that outcome too: target-account preparation, outreach, response handling, follow-up, qualification, CRM workflow, reporting, and campaign improvement.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How much do outsourced SDR and BDR services cost?</summary><p>CallTeam managed outbound programs start at US$4,000 per month for a campaign-ready company with a clear offer, defined market, target accounts or contacts ready to activate, CRM and calendar access, and a sales team ready for meetings. Fresh prospect research, data, additional markets, and expanded capacity are priced into the final scope.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Does the starting price include a new prospect list?</summary><p>The US$4,000 starting program assumes target accounts or contact data are ready to activate. CallTeam can build or refine a prospect list when needed. Research, data licensing, validation, and list volume are priced into the final scope.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Who manages the campaign and approves the messaging?</summary><p>CallTeam manages the agreed daily execution, follow-up, qualification, reporting, and improvement. Your team approves the offer, claims, proof, talk track, qualification questions, and meeting standard. You also provide sales availability and handle opportunities after handoff.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How does CallTeam qualify a meeting?</summary><p>We agree the standard before launch. It can include company fit, buyer role, business need, current approach, interest, timing, decision process, and a clear purpose for the next conversation. The buyer must understand and accept that next step.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam work inside our CRM?</summary><p>Yes, with agreed access, permissions, fields, and operating rules. We confirm how records, outcomes, notes, and next actions reach your team before launch. If direct CRM access is unsuitable, we agree another structured reporting and handoff process.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do outsourced SDRs and BDRs use cold calling or email?</summary><p>CallTeam is calling-led. Live conversations help establish fit, objections, referrals, timing, and interest. Approved email follow-up and other agreed channels can support the campaign. The channel mix, infrastructure, permissions, and boundaries are defined in the scope.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Is the outreach done by people or AI?</summary><p>People handle CallTeam sales conversations, objections, qualification, and next-step agreement. AI can assist with account research, data organization, priorities, call preparation, and note structure. Human judgment stays central to the conversation.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How quickly can an outsourced SDR campaign launch?</summary><p>The launch date depends on the readiness of your offer, audience, contact data, approvals, systems, and calendars. We review those inputs and agree a launch plan before execution. Research or workflow setup can add preparation time.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How long is the initial engagement?</summary><p>Most CallTeam managed outbound programs begin with an initial three-month engagement. That allows time to launch, learn from buyer conversations, refine the campaign, and assess meaningful results. The scope and terms are agreed before work begins.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What reporting will we receive?</summary><p>Reporting is agreed for the engagement and connects activity to conversations, qualification, meetings, follow-up, and market feedback. Weekly reporting is included in the starting managed program. Opportunity updates from your sales team help show what happens after the handoff.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Which companies and markets does CallTeam support?</summary><p>CallTeam supports B2B companies in Canada, the United States, and international markets. Relevant engagements include SaaS, technology, cybersecurity, financial services, professional services, and market expansion. Each campaign is scoped around its offer, target buyers, geography, and qualification needs.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Can CallTeam follow up with inbound or dormant leads?</summary><p>Yes, an agreed engagement can work with inbound inquiries, event lists, dormant opportunities, or existing CRM contacts as well as new target accounts. We define the response workflow, priority, qualification, and handoff for that audience before launch.</p></details>
        <details><summary>When should we hire an internal SDR instead?</summary><p>An internal team can be a better fit when you have a proven playbook, dedicated sales development leadership, enough ongoing work, and the ability to recruit, train, equip, and coach the team. Outsourcing fits companies that want the agreed front-end sales work managed externally.</p></details>
        <details><summary>How do we get started?</summary><p>Book a strategy call and tell us what you sell, who buys it, where you want to grow, and what sales development work needs support. CallTeam reviews your market, data, qualification standard, systems, and sales capacity, then recommends the scope.</p></details>
